<title>SINGAPORE: Hewlett-Packard launches Java desktop.</title>
<headline>Hewlett-Packard launches Java desktop.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hewlett-Packard Co on Wednesday launched its first desktop computer powered by Java, an open-platform software developed by Sun Microsystems.</p>
<p>The desktop was introduced by Hewlett-Packard Singapore (Sales) Pte Ltd and SunSoft Asia South, at Comdex/Asia, a computer exhibition held in Singapore.</p>
<p>The HP Vectra Java powered personal computer comes with SunSoft Java Workshop, a multi-platform development tool for creating applications on the Internet.</p>
<p>The PCs available in Vectra VL4 models Pentium 100, 133 and 166, comes with Windows 95.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
